# Files and directories that are left out of the distributable plugin package.
#
# Read by `wp dist-archive` and by WordPress.org deploy tools. One path or
# pattern per line; a leading slash anchors it to the plugin root. List
# exclusions only: some of these tools do not support negation.
#
# The release workflow builds its package from an allowlist.
# .github/scripts/check-plugin-package.py fails when this file and that
# allowlist would ship different tracked files, and when a shipped file breaks
# a rule below, so keep the two in step.

# --- What the WordPress.org plugin directory does not accept ---------------
# (the file rules of the Plugin Check plugin)

# Hidden files and directories. This covers version control (.git, .svn),
# repository automation (.github), editor and AI-tool directories (.vscode,
# .idea, .claude, .cursor), tool configuration, caches, and this file.
.*

# Compressed archives
*.7z
*.gz
*.rar
*.tar
*.tgz
*.zip

# PHP archives, executables, scripts, and other application files
*.phar
*.a
*.bin
*.bpk
*.deploy
*.dist
*.distz
*.dmg
*.dms
*.dump
*.elc
*.exe
*.iso
*.lha
*.lrf
*.lzh
*.o
*.obj
*.pkg
*.sh
*.so

# --- What this project leaves out as well ----------------------------------

# Markdown. The package carries readme.txt, which holds the description and
# the changelog; no .md file ships.
*.md

# Development tooling and its configuration
/.markdownlint.json
/.yamllint.yml
/composer.json
/composer.lock
/phpcs.xml
/phpmd.xml
/phpstan.neon
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/phpunit.xml
/psalm.xml
/renovate.json
/bin
/stubs
/tests

# Dependencies, caches, and build output
/vendor
/node_modules
/build
/coverage
/dist
/plugin-check-build
__pycache__
Thumbs.db
*.log
*.sql
*.swp
*~
